  "Id": "83a94bb9-64ef-5d72-93c9-2e8795126b04"/*PhysicsBouncingBallsExample*/,
  "Description": "Five balls dropped from the same height with Bounciness from 0 to 1.\n\nEach [RigidBody] sphere carries its own Bounciness. The left ball lands dead, the right one rebounds almost to its starting height. The balls are drawn with [DrawMeshAtPoints] from the point buffer of [PhysicsWorld].\n\nAKA: restitution, bounce, rubber ball\n\nTips\n- Set Reset on [PhysicsWorld] to drop the balls again.\n- Raise Bounciness and Friction on the ground as well; a pair uses the larger Bounciness of the two bodies.",
